Please note that nominees are not to be informed of their nomination until after the winners are announced. If you have any questions, contact hr@hartfieldgroup.com.

The HR Team
Hartfield Group','triple passage');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n23000ve3wcgm17jmsk',7,'What is the purpose of the first document?','To announce the winners of an employee award','To invite nominations for an annual recognition event','To describe the history of the Hartfield Group','To request feedback on last year''s gala','B','첫 번째 문서(공지문)는 직원 인정 시상식 행사에 대한 후보 지명 공고입니다. ''nominations are now open''이 핵심 표현입니다. ① 수상자 발표는 행사 당일, ③ 회사 역사는 언급 없음, ④ 피드백 요청도 없습니다.','','cmqqb0n23000ue3wciegzxbu5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n23000we3wcbpjpfsxa',7,'For which award category is Dr. Lim being nominated?','Leadership','Customer Excellence','Team Collaboration','Innovation','D','두 번째 문서(Marcus의 이메일)에서 ''I would like to nominate Dr. Sarah Lim for the Innovation award''라고 명시되어 있습니다. 다른 카테고리(Leadership, Customer Excellence, Team Collaboration)는 첫 번째 문서에 나열되어 있지만 Dr. Lim의 카테고리는 Innovation입니다.','','cmqqb0n23000ue3wciegzxbu5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n23000xe3wc249bxc6c',7,'By what date must nominations be submitted?','September 15','September 19','September 30','October 3','B','첫 번째 문서에 ''Nominations must be submitted...by September 19''라고 명시되어 있습니다. September 15는 Marcus가 이메일을 보낸 날짜, September 30은 노미니에게 통보하는 날짜, October 3는 RSVP 마감일입니다.','','cmqqb0n23000ue3wciegzxbu5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n23000ye3wc6bwayqd8',7,'What did Dr. Lim accomplish according to Mr. Reynolds?','She increased the company''s client base by 18 percent','She reduced production costs by 18 percent while improving quality','She developed a new training program for engineers','She led a successful international expansion project','B','두 번째 문서에서 ''reducing production costs by 18 percent while improving output quality''라고 명시되어 있습니다. ① 고객 기반 증가는 언급 없음, ③ 교육 프로그램도 언급 없음, ④ 해외 확장도 언급되지 않았습니다.','','cmqqb0n23000ue3wciegzxbu5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n23000ze3wcsfkuo82k',7,'What should Mr. Reynolds NOT do according to the third document?','Contact HR if he has questions','Inform Dr. Lim that she has been nominated','Wait for the committee''s decision','Attend the ceremony on October 17','B','세 번째 문서(확인 이메일)에 ''nominees are not to be informed of their nomination until after the winners are announced''라고 명시되어 있습니다. 수상자 발표 전까지 피추천인에게 알려서는 안 됩니다. 나머지 선택지는 금지 사항이 아닙니다.','','cmqqb0n23000ue3wciegzxbu5');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcayp60000xkwcbq49rgcu',6,'To: All Staff
From: IT Department
Subject: System Maintenance Update
Date: March 14

We would like to inform all employees that our company''s internal network will undergo a scheduled upgrade this coming Saturday, from 10 P.M. to 6 A.M. Sunday. ___131___ all files and documents before Friday evening to avoid any potential data loss.

The upgrade is ___132___ to significantly improve network speed and security features across all departments. Staff members who need to access work-related files during the maintenance window are advised to download the necessary documents to their local drives beforehand.

Please be aware that e-mail services will be temporarily unavailable during this period. ___133___ Any urgent communications should be handled via mobile phone during this time.

___134___ We appreciate your understanding and cooperation in this matter.

The IT Department','email');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp70001xkwcq8rjweut',6,'___131___','Please backing up','Please to back up','Please back up','Please backed up','C','[Please + 동사원형] 명령문에서 Please 뒤에는 동사원형(back up)이 옵니다. ④ backed up은 과거형입니다. ① backing up은 현재분사입니다. ② to back up은 to부정사로 명령문에 쓸 수 없습니다.','','cmqqcayp60000xkwcbq49rgcu');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp70002xkwc87uul687',6,'___132___','expects','expected','expecting','expectation','B','[is expected] be + 과거분사 구조의 수동태입니다. ''is expected to + 동사원형''은 ''~할 것으로 예상된다''는 표현입니다. ③ expecting은 능동 진행형입니다. ④ expectation은 명사입니다. ① expects는 3인칭 능동형입니다.','','cmqqcayp60000xkwcbq49rgcu');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp70003xkwcchb8tqd6',6,'___133___','This includes access to the company intranet and shared drives.','Employees are encouraged to work overtime during the upgrade.','The IT team is currently hiring additional technicians.','Please contact the IT department to install the new software.','A','[문맥 파악] 앞 문장에서 이메일 서비스가 일시적으로 사용 불가능하다고 했습니다. 이어서 그 범위를 구체화하는 (A) ''인트라넷과 공유 드라이브 접속 포함''이 자연스럽게 이어집니다.','','cmqqcayp60000xkwcbq49rgcu');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp70004xkwcj8wo0n61',6,'___134___','The system has been successfully upgraded as planned.','We regret to inform you that the project has been canceled.','All staff must complete the online safety training by next month.','Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us.','D','[마무리 문장] 공지 이메일의 마지막 부분으로, 질문이 있으면 연락 달라는 (A)가 ''감사드린다''는 마무리 문장 앞에 자연스럽게 위치합니다.','','cmqqcayp60000xkwcbq49rgcu');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcayp90005xkwcaw7n260m',6,'May 3

Ms. Rachel Oduya
Director of Operations
Pinnacle Solutions Ltd.

Dear Ms. Oduya,

On behalf of the Westbridge Chamber of Commerce, I am writing to ___135___ you to our upcoming Annual Business Leadership Forum, scheduled for June 15–16 at the Riverside Convention Center.

This year''s forum will feature keynote ___136___ from executives at leading companies across the region. Topics will include sustainable business practices, digital transformation, and talent management strategies.

As a valued member of our business community, we believe your ___137___ would be invaluable to our discussions. Attendance is complimentary for chamber members.

To reserve your seat, please visit our website at www.westbridgechamber.org/forum or contact our office at 555-8472. ___138___ We look forward to your participation.

Sincerely,

James Whitfield
Executive Director, Westbridge Chamber of Commerce','letter');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp90006xkwczz604cqd',6,'___135___','invited','inviting','invite','invitation','C','[to + 동사원형] ''am writing to invite''는 ''초청하기 위해 편지를 씁니다''의 의미입니다. ④ invitation은 명사입니다. ① invited는 과거분사입니다. ② inviting은 현재분사입니다.','','cmqqcayp90005xkwcaw7n260m');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp90007xkwcjavaet59',6,'___136___','presently','presentations','present','presentable','B','[명사] ''feature keynote ___''에서 목적어 자리에 명사 presentations(발표들)이 적절합니다. ③ present는 문맥상 부적절합니다. ④ presentable은 형용사입니다. ① presently는 부사입니다.','','cmqqcayp90005xkwcaw7n260m');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp90008xkwcgxx8o2rj',6,'___137___','participation','participate','participatory','participated','A','[명사] 소유격 your 뒤에는 명사(participation: 참여)가 옵니다. ② participate는 동사입니다. ③ participatory는 형용사입니다. ④ participated는 과거형 동사입니다.','','cmqqcayp90005xkwcaw7n260m');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcayp90009xkwcbpu62fyg',6,'___138___','The forum will take place every year without exception.','Our previous forum was attended by fewer participants than expected.','Please note that all speakers must submit their presentations in advance.','Registration closes on June 1, so we encourage you to sign up early.','D','[문맥 파악] 등록 방법을 안내한 직후에 마감일 알림과 조기 등록 권고가 이어지는 (A)가 가장 자연스럽습니다.','','cmqqcayp90005xkwcaw7n260m');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcaypb000axkwcq25kvkdw',7,'Kingsley Office Park – Parking Policy Update

Effective September 1, Kingsley Office Park will be implementing a new parking management system to better serve all tenants. Key changes include the following:

• Assigned Parking: Each business unit will be allocated a set number of dedicated parking spaces based on office size. Assignments will be sent to all tenants by August 15.

• Visitor Parking: A designated visitor lot (Lot C) will be available for guest parking only. Tenants and their employees are not permitted to park in Lot C at any time.

• Parking Permits: All regular parkers must display a valid permit on their dashboard. Permits can be picked up at the property management office (Suite 102) starting August 20.

• After-Hours Parking: The parking structure will remain accessible 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. However, overnight parking (from 10 P.M. to 6 A.M.) requires prior approval from building management.

Tenants with questions or concerns are encouraged to contact the property management office at park@kingsleyofficepk.com.','notice');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypb000bxkwc98pzp1jy',7,'What is the purpose of the announcement?','To announce the opening of a new parking structure','To request feedback from tenants about current facilities','To inform tenants about changes to a parking system','To advertise available office spaces in the building','C','첫 문장에서 ''new parking management system''을 시행할 것을 알린다고 했습니다. 전체적으로 주차 시스템 변경 내용을 안내하는 공지입니다.','','cmqqcaypb000axkwcq25kvkdw');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypb000cxkwcsqw8u798',7,'According to the announcement, where can employees pick up their parking permits?','Online through the company website','At the property management office','At the main entrance of the building','By contacting the tenants directly','B','''Permits can be picked up at the property management office (Suite 102)''라고 명시되어 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypb000axkwcq25kvkdw');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypb000dxkwca19b6yad',7,'What restriction applies to overnight parking?','It requires approval from building management.','It is not permitted under any circumstances.','It is available only to business owners.','It must be arranged two weeks in advance.','A','''overnight parking (from 10 P.M. to 6 A.M.) requires prior approval from building management''라고 명시되어 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypb000axkwcq25kvkdw');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000exkwctyvk9idg',7,'Workplace Wellness Pays Off

A recent survey conducted by the Global Workforce Institute revealed that companies investing in employee wellness programs see an average 23 percent reduction in absenteeism and a 17 percent improvement in overall productivity. The findings are prompting many businesses to revisit their benefit offerings.

"We noticed a clear link between employee health and output," said Sandra Meyering, Human Resources Director at Calloway Manufacturing. "After launching our wellness initiative two years ago, which includes on-site fitness classes, mental health counseling, and flexible scheduling, our annual turnover rate dropped from 18 percent to just 9 percent."

The survey polled over 2,400 companies across 14 countries. Respondents indicated that nutrition workshops, stress management programs, and subsidized gym memberships were among the most popular offerings. Notably, remote employees were 35 percent less likely to participate in wellness programs than office-based workers, suggesting that companies need to develop virtual wellness solutions.

Industry analysts predict that the demand for comprehensive wellness packages will continue to grow as younger generations increasingly prioritize work-life balance when choosing an employer.','article');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000fxkwceqrcbhwg',7,'What is the main topic of the article?','The challenges of managing remote workers','The results of a government health initiative','The growing cost of healthcare for employers','The business benefits of employee wellness programs','D','첫 문단부터 직원 웰니스 프로그램 투자의 이점(결근율 감소, 생산성 향상)을 소개하며 전체 기사가 이를 다루고 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypd000exkwctyvk9idg');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000gxkwc8gnk1sf8',7,'What happened at Calloway Manufacturing after launching its wellness initiative?','Its productivity dropped by 17 percent.','Its HR department was restructured.','Its employee turnover rate decreased significantly.','It reduced its number of wellness programs.','C','''our annual turnover rate dropped from 18 percent to just 9 percent''라고 Sandra Meyering이 언급했습니다.','','cmqqcaypd000exkwctyvk9idg');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000hxkwcdfi0n6ng',7,'What challenge related to remote employees is mentioned in the article?','They prefer in-office work over remote arrangements.','They are less likely to take part in wellness programs.','They are more prone to workplace injuries.','They tend to change jobs more frequently.','B','''remote employees were 35 percent less likely to participate in wellness programs than office-based workers''라고 명시되어 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypd000exkwctyvk9idg');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000ixkwctr9510qp',7,'What does the article suggest about future trends?','Demand for wellness benefits will keep increasing.','Younger workers will prioritize higher salaries over wellness.','Virtual wellness solutions have already become standard.','The survey results will be revised after further research.','A','''demand for comprehensive wellness packages will continue to grow''라고 마지막 단락에서 예측하고 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypd000exkwctyvk9idg');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcaypd000jxkwc998xa5de',7,'Online Chat Discussion

Laura Kim [10:14 A.M.]
Good morning, everyone. The vendor for tomorrow''s product launch event just called. They''re saying they can''t deliver the display panels until 3 P.M. Our setup was scheduled for 10 A.M.

Marcus Lee [10:16 A.M.]
That''s a problem. The press conference starts at 5 P.M. sharp. Do we have enough time to set everything up by then?

Laura Kim [10:18 A.M.]
It will be tight. I need to notify the AV team to adjust their schedule. Also, the catering company needs to know about the change.

Dana Ortega [10:20 A.M.]
I''ll reach out to the caterers right away. They mentioned they were flexible on timing.

Marcus Lee [10:23 A.M.]
Good. Laura, should we also contact the venue manager? They might need to reschedule the room setup crew.

Laura Kim [10:25 A.M.]
Yes, please handle that, Marcus. I''ll get the AV team sorted. Dana, once you''ve spoken to the caterers, can you send me a quick update?

Dana Ortega [10:27 A.M.]
Of course. I''ll message you as soon as I have confirmation.','notice');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaype000kxkwcjzslweqd',7,'Why is the group having a discussion?','A press conference was canceled at the last minute.','The AV equipment was damaged during transport.','The catering company changed their menu options.','A vendor notified them of a delayed delivery.','D','Laura Kim의 첫 메시지에서 납품업체가 디스플레이 패널을 오후 3시에야 배달할 수 있다고 알립니다.','','cmqqcaypd000jxkwc998xa5de');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaype000lxkwckepe5rco',7,'What will Marcus Lee most likely do next?','Reschedule the press conference','Call the display panel vendor','Contact the venue manager','Speak with the catering company','C','10:25 A.M.에 Laura가 Marcus에게 ''please handle that''(= contact the venue manager)라고 부탁했습니다.','','cmqqcaypd000jxkwc998xa5de');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaype000mxkwc7xxaxsly',7,'At 10:27 A.M., what does Dana Ortega most likely mean when she writes, ''I''ll message you as soon as I have confirmation''?','She will confirm the delivery time with the vendor.','She will update Laura after speaking with the caterers.','She will contact the AV team on Laura''s behalf.','She will send an invitation to the press conference.','B','Dana는 케이터링 업체에 연락한 후 Laura에게 결과를 알리겠다고 했습니다. Laura가 요청한 ''quick update''에 대한 답변입니다.','','cmqqcaypd000jxkwc998xa5de');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcaypf000nxkwc62ckh6er',7,'LensPerfect Photography Studio – Services & Packages

At LensPerfect, we specialize in:
• Corporate headshots and team photos
• Product photography for e-commerce and advertising
• Event coverage (conferences, award ceremonies, company parties)
• Real estate and architectural photography

STANDARD – $350
Up to 2 hours of shooting | 30 edited digital images | Online gallery for 60 days

PROFESSIONAL – $650
Up to 4 hours of shooting | 75 edited digital images | Online gallery for 90 days | Priority editing (delivered within 5 business days)

PREMIUM – $1,100
Full-day shooting (up to 8 hours) | Unlimited edited images | Online gallery for 12 months | Same-day preview | Dedicated photo editor

All sessions include a pre-shoot consultation at no additional charge.
Contact: info@lensperfect.com | 555-3140','double passage');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypi000pxkwc6acfrhb2',7,'What type of photography service does LensPerfect NOT offer?','Wedding photography','Corporate team photos','Product photography','Event coverage','A','웹페이지에 나열된 서비스는 Corporate headshots, Product photography, Event coverage, Real estate입니다. Wedding photography(웨딩 사진)는 언급되어 있지 않습니다.','','cmqqcaypf000nxkwc62ckh6er');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypi000qxkwcz6x13d78',7,'Which package is Mr. Ellerton most likely interested in?','The Professional package','The Standard package','A custom package not listed','The Premium package','D','이메일에서 Mr. Ellerton은 하루 종일 촬영, 1년 이상 이미지 보관, 당일 미리보기를 원하며 ''your top-tier package''라고 직접 언급했습니다. 이는 PREMIUM 패키지입니다.','','cmqqcaypf000nxkwc62ckh6er');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "QuestionGroup" ("id","part","passageText","passageType") VALUES ('cmqqcaypg000oxkwcx7swh5y1',7,'From: James Ellerton <j.ellerton@novatech-solutions.com>
To: info@lensperfect.com
Date: October 8
Subject: Photography Services Inquiry

Dear LensPerfect Team,

I am the marketing manager at NovaTech Solutions, and we are planning our annual company event on November 3. We would like to hire a professional photographer to cover the entire day, from the morning team-building activities starting at 9 A.M. through to the evening awards ceremony ending at approximately 7 P.M.

We require all images to be available to us for at least a year, and we would find it very helpful to see some preliminary shots on the day itself. Additionally, as we plan to use the photos for our company website and promotional materials, high-quality editing is essential.

Based on your website, I believe your top-tier package would best meet our needs. However, I was wondering if you could accommodate one additional request: we would like a dedicated editor who specializes in corporate event photography.

Please let me know if this is possible and whether you are available on November 3.

Best regards,
James Ellerton','double passage');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypj000rxkwc07w8cf92',7,'What additional request does Mr. Ellerton make that is not listed in any package?','Same-day delivery of all edited photos','A discounted rate for a large event','A dedicated editor specializing in corporate events','An extended online gallery period','C','Mr. Ellerton은 ''a dedicated editor who specializes in corporate event photography''를 요청했는데, 이는 패키지에 명시되지 않은 추가 요구사항입니다.','','cmqqcaypg000oxkwcx7swh5y1');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypk000sxkwchkv2xc5i',7,'What is implied about the pre-shoot consultation?','It takes place at the client''s office or location.','Customers do not pay extra for it.','It is only available for the Premium package.','It must be completed at least two weeks in advance.','B','''All sessions include a pre-shoot consultation at no additional charge''라고 명시되어 있어 추가 비용이 없음을 알 수 있습니다.','','cmqqcaypg000oxkwcx7swh5y1');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqcaypk000txkwcb5s2uro4',7,'What is the purpose of Mr. Ellerton''s e-mail?','To inquire about availability and a special request','To confirm a booking made over the phone','To request a refund for a previous session','To apply for a job at LensPerfect','A','이메일은 11월 3일 예약 가능 여부를 묻고 추가 요청 사항이 가능한지 질의하는 내용입니다.','','cmqqcaypg000oxkwcx7swh5y1');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n100000e3wcfktu8vyw',5,'The accounting department _______ every financial record since the new audit regulations took effect last year.','verifies','verified','has verified','to verify','C','[현재완료] ''since + 과거 절''이 오면 반드시 현재완료(have/has + p.p.)를 써야 합니다. ''since the regulations took effect''는 과거 시점을 나타내므로 has verified가 유일하게 맞는 시제입니다. ① verifies는 단순 현재로 since와 함께 쓸 수 없고, ② verified는 단순 과거로 since절과 함께 현재완료에서 써야 합니다, ④ to verify는 부정사로 주어의 동사 자리에 올 수 없습니다.','동사 시제',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n110001e3wcdzlu0co0',5,'All visitors must sign in _______ the security counter on the ground floor before proceeding upstairs.','on','in','at','by','C','[전치사 at] 특정 지점(카운터, 책상, 입구)에서 무언가를 ''하다''라는 표현에는 at을 씁니다. sign in at the counter = ''카운터에서 서명하다''. ① on은 표면 위(on the counter), ② in은 공간 내부(in the building), ④ by는 ''~옆에'' 또는 수단을 나타내며 여기에는 적합하지 않습니다.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n120002e3wcagxsc2qw',5,'Employees should submit _______ completed evaluation forms to the HR department no later than Friday.','they','them','their','theirs','C','[소유격 대명사] 명사(forms) 앞에서 소유를 나타내는 역할은 소유격(their)만 가능합니다. ① they는 주격 대명사, ② them은 목적격 대명사, ④ theirs는 독립 소유대명사로 뒤에 명사를 수식할 수 없습니다. 빈칸 뒤에 명사가 있으면 반드시 소유격을 선택하세요.','대명사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n130003e3wcm3n2qqvw',5,'Customer satisfaction scores for the new product line have been _______ high, exceeding all internal benchmarks.','remark','remarkable','remarkably','remarked','C','[부사] 형용사(high)를 수식하려면 부사가 필요합니다. remarkably(부사)가 정답입니다. ① remark는 동사/명사, ② remarkable은 형용사로 명사만 수식할 수 있습니다, ④ remarked는 동사 과거형입니다. ''부사 + 형용사'' 구조를 기억하세요.','품사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n130004e3wcpo8b9gvr',5,'_______ the significant budget cuts, the marketing team successfully launched three new campaigns this quarter.','Although','Because','Despite','However','C','[전치사 Despite] 빈칸 뒤에 명사구(the significant budget cuts)가 오므로 전치사 Despite(~에도 불구하고)가 필요합니다. ① Although는 접속사로 반드시 ''주어+동사'' 절이 필요합니다(Although the budget was cut), ② Because도 접속사, ④ However는 부사로 명사구 앞에 올 수 없습니다.','전치사/접속사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n160005e3wcicf9pqcb',5,'The three finalists _______ scored above 90 percent on the written assessment will advance to the final interview round.','whose','which','whom','who','D','[주격 관계대명사 who] 선행사가 사람(finalists)이고 관계절 안에서 주어 역할(scored)을 하므로 주격 관계대명사 who가 정답입니다. ① whose는 소유격(whose score was...), ② which는 사물에 사용, ③ whom은 목적격(whom the company selected)입니다.','관계대명사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n160006e3wclb8jwwn9',5,'The final version of the annual report _______ by the editorial team before it is distributed to shareholders.','reviews','will review','will be reviewed','reviewing','C','[수동태] 연간 보고서(report)는 검토를 ''받는'' 대상이므로 수동태가 필요합니다. will be reviewed = ''검토될 것이다''. ① reviews와 ② will review는 능동태로 보고서가 스스로 검토한다는 비논리적 의미가 됩니다. ④ reviewing은 보조동사 없이 단독으로 술어 동사가 될 수 없습니다.','수동태',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n170007e3wcbm6ci4mx',5,'The factory has maintained a perfect safety record _______ the new workplace safety protocols were introduced in January.','for','during','since','while','C','[since + 과거 시점] 빈칸 뒤에 과거 시점을 나타내는 절(were introduced in January)이 오고 현재완료(has maintained)와 함께 사용되므로 since(~이후로)가 정답입니다. ① for는 기간의 길이(for six months) 앞에 쓰며 절 앞에는 올 수 없습니다. ② during과 ④ while은 ''~동안''으로 다른 용법입니다.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n170008e3wcv0vv1438',5,'The board of directors voted in favor of the _______ of two additional overseas branches next fiscal year.','open','openly','opened','opening','D','[명사 자리] 전치사 of 앞, 관사(the) 뒤에는 명사가 와야 합니다. opening은 동명사/명사로 ''개설''을 의미합니다. ① open은 형용사/동사, ② openly는 부사, ③ opened는 과거형 동사입니다. the + [명사] + of 구조에서 명사를 고르는 문제입니다.','품사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n180009e3wch5lbni8s',5,'The new cloud-based software processes data _______ more efficiently than any previous system the company has used.','very','quite','much','so','C','[비교급 강조] 비교급(more efficiently)을 강조할 때는 much, far, even, a lot을 씁니다. ① very는 원급 형용사·부사 강조에만 쓰이며 비교급 앞에 올 수 없습니다. ② quite와 ④ so도 비교급 강조 용도로 쓰이지 않습니다. much more efficiently = ''훨씬 더 효율적으로''.','부사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n18000ae3wcn5u2v1jm',5,'Construction workers will continue laying the foundation _______ the structural engineer gives final approval.','before','unless','until','although','C','[until] ''최종 승인이 날 때까지 계속 작업한다''는 의미이므로 until(~할 때까지)이 정답입니다. ① before는 ''~하기 전에 멈춘다''는 의미로 continue와 어울리지 않습니다. ② unless는 ''~하지 않으면'', ④ although는 ''~에도 불구하고''로 문맥에 맞지 않습니다.','접속사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n19000be3wcjouo3i0w',5,'The keynote speaker delivered an _______ presentation that motivated all attendees to take immediate action.','inspire','inspiration','inspirational','inspired','C','[형용사] 명사(presentation)를 수식하는 자리이므로 형용사가 필요합니다. inspirational(영감을 주는)이 정답입니다. ④ inspired는 ''영감을 받은(수동)'' 의미로 발표가 영감을 ''받았다''는 뜻이 되어 부적절합니다. ① inspire는 동사, ② inspiration은 명사입니다.','품사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n19000ce3wciycvmmrs',5,'Parcels _______ to the wrong address must be returned to the distribution center within 48 hours.','deliver','delivering','delivered','delivery','C','[과거분사 - 수동 수식] 소포(Parcels)는 배달을 ''받는'' 대상이므로 과거분사 delivered(배달된)가 명사를 수식합니다. ② delivering은 현재분사로 ''소포가 배달하고 있다''는 능동 의미가 되어 부적절합니다. ① deliver는 동사 원형, ④ delivery는 명사입니다.','분사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n19000de3wceb9kba13',5,'Ms. Harrison has been leading the company''s sustainability initiatives _______ over a decade.','since','during','for','within','C','[for + 기간] ''over a decade(10년 이상)''은 기간의 길이를 나타내므로 for를 씁니다. ① since는 특정 시점(since 2015) 앞에 쓰며, 뒤에 숫자 기간이 오지 않습니다. ② during은 사건/기간의 이름 앞에(during the project), ④ within은 ''~이내에(within 3 days)''의 의미입니다.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1a000ee3wchbrp2nug',5,'The safety equipment was _______ tested by an independent laboratory before being approved for use.','thorough','thoroughly','thoroughness','more thorough','B','[부사] 과거분사(tested)를 수식하는 자리이므로 부사가 필요합니다. thoroughly(철저하게)가 정답입니다. ① thorough는 형용사로 명사를 수식합니다. ③ thoroughness는 명사, ④ more thorough는 형용사 비교급으로 동사/분사를 직접 수식할 수 없습니다.','품사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1a000fe3wcxs5ft400',5,'The operations manager is responsible for _______ that all safety guidelines are followed on the production floor.','ensure','ensures','ensured','ensuring','D','[전치사 뒤 동명사] ''responsible for'' 뒤에는 반드시 동명사(-ing)가 와야 합니다. 전치사(for) 뒤에는 동명사가 오는 것이 영문법의 핵심 원칙입니다. ① ensure는 동사 원형, ② ensures는 3인칭 단수 동사, ③ ensured는 과거형/과거분사로 전치사 뒤에 올 수 없습니다.','동명사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1a000ge3wcpxu5j6zw',5,'The renovation was completed two weeks _______ schedule, allowing the store to open earlier than anticipated.','ahead of','in front of','prior than','before of','A','[관용 표현] ahead of schedule은 ''예정보다 일찍''을 뜻하는 고정 표현입니다. ② in front of는 물리적 위치(앞에 있는), ③ prior than은 영어에서 존재하지 않는 표현(prior to가 올바름), ④ before of도 존재하지 않는 표현입니다. ahead of schedule은 TOEIC 빈출 숙어로 반드시 암기하세요.','관용어구',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1b000he3wczcqljj92',5,'The company hired three bilingual assistants _______ support its growing international client base.','for','so that','to','in order that','C','[to부정사 - 목적] 동사 hired의 목적(지원하기 위해)을 나타낼 때 to 부정사를 씁니다. to support = ''지원하기 위해''. ① for 뒤에는 명사(구), ② so that과 ④ in order that은 접속사로 반드시 ''주어 + 동사'' 절이 이어져야 합니다(so that they could support...).','to부정사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1c000ie3wcte3wjr9a',5,'Every employee in the department _______ expected to complete the mandatory compliance training by month-end.','are','is','were','have been','B','[Every + 단수 동사] ''Every + 단수 명사''는 반드시 단수 동사와 함께 씁니다. Every employee = 단수 주어 → is expected. ① are와 ③ were는 복수/과거 동사, ④ have been은 복수 주어에 쓰는 현재완료입니다. ''Every/Each + 명사 + 단수 동사''는 절대적인 규칙입니다.','수일치',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1c000je3wchxktg20i',5,'The new facility is designed to be spacious, energy-efficient, and _______ for employees with mobility challenges.','accessibility','access','accessible','accessing','C','[병렬구조 - 형용사] and로 연결된 spacious(형용사), energy-efficient(형용사)와 나란히 형용사 accessible(접근 가능한)이 와야 합니다. ① accessibility는 명사, ② access는 명사/동사, ④ accessing은 현재분사/동명사로 형용사와 병렬을 이루지 못합니다.','병렬구조',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1c000ke3wcnrm5we89',5,'All grant applications must be received _______ 5 P.M. on the closing date to be considered for funding.','until','unless','by','throughout','C','[by - 기한] by는 특정 시점까지 완료해야 하는 ''기한''을 나타냅니다. by 5 P.M. = ''오후 5시까지''. ① until은 동작의 지속(keep open until 5 P.M.)을 나타내며 완료 기한에는 쓰지 않습니다. received until은 ''5시까지 계속 받는다''는 의미가 되어 맥락상 어색합니다. ② unless는 조건, ④ throughout은 ''~내내''.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1d000le3wcfmkpgqg6',5,'The regional director had the quarterly performance data _______ before presenting it to the executive team.','compile','compiling','compiled','to compile','C','[사역동사 have + 목적어 + p.p.] ''have + 목적어 + 과거분사''는 ''목적어가 ~되게 하다(수동)''를 나타냅니다. 데이터(data)는 누군가에 의해 ''컴파일되는'' 대상이므로 과거분사 compiled가 정답입니다. ① compile은 목적어가 능동으로 행동할 때(have staff compile), ② compiling도 능동 관계, ④ to compile은 이 구조에서 쓰이지 않습니다.','사역동사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1e000me3wck0y2x44r',5,'The _______ of the new high-speed rail line has transformed commuting times across the entire region.','open','openly','opening','opened','C','[명사 자리 - 동명사/명사] ''The + _____ + of''에서 빈칸은 명사 자리입니다. opening(개통, 개장)이 명사로 정답입니다. ① open은 형용사/동사, ② openly는 부사, ④ opened는 동사 과거형으로 명사 자리에 올 수 없습니다. open → opening의 품사 변환을 기억하세요.','품사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1e000ne3wcqpiyalut',5,'Interns may use the company''s video conferencing tools _______ they obtain prior approval from their supervisor.','even if','as long as','unless','in case','B','[as long as - 조건] as long as = ''~하는 한, ~하기만 하면'' (조건부 허가). ① even if는 ''~에도 불구하고(허가)''로 조건 없이 허락한다는 의미가 되어 문맥 불일치. ③ unless는 ''승인받지 않으면 쓸 수 없다''는 뜻이 되어 반대 의미. ④ in case는 ''~에 대비해서(예방 목적)''로 허가 조건을 나타내지 않습니다.','접속사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1i000oe3wc7wxtjmbr',5,'The company''s 50th anniversary celebration is scheduled to take place _______ Saturday, June 14, at the downtown convention center.','in','at','by','on','D','[on + 요일/날짜] 요일(Saturday)이나 특정 날짜(June 14) 앞에는 항상 on을 씁니다. ① in은 월·연도·계절 앞(in June, in 2026), ② at은 시각 앞(at 9 A.M., at noon), ③ by는 기한을 나타냅니다. on Saturday / on June 14 처럼 요일·날짜 앞에는 예외 없이 on입니다.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1k000pe3wc5in66fif',5,'Staff members should _______ their timesheets through the new payroll portal each Friday by noon.','submitted','submitting','submit','to submit','C','[조동사 + 동사원형] 조동사(should, must, can, will 등) 뒤에는 반드시 동사원형이 옵니다. submit(제출하다)이 정답입니다. ① submitted는 과거형/과거분사, ② submitting은 현재분사, ④ to submit은 to 부정사로 모두 조동사 바로 뒤에 올 수 없습니다.','조동사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1l000qe3wc0ipohtmc',5,'The partnership agreement will benefit _______ the domestic suppliers and the overseas distribution partners.','either','neither','both','not only','C','[both A and B] ''both A and B''는 ''A와 B 모두''를 의미합니다. both the domestic suppliers and the overseas partners = 양측 모두 혜택을 받는다. ① either A or B는 ''둘 중 하나'', ② neither A nor B는 ''둘 다 아님'', ④ not only는 ''not only A but also B'' 구조를 완성해야 합니다.','상관접속사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1m000re3wc55ove7pb',5,'The storage area is not wide _______ to accommodate the new industrial shelving units ordered last month.','too','enough','very','quite','B','[형용사/부사 + enough + to] ''~할 만큼 충분히 ~한''은 형용사/부사 + enough + to 부정사 구조입니다. wide enough to accommodate = ''수납할 만큼 충분히 넓은''. ① too + 형용사 + to는 ''너무 ~해서 ~할 수 없다(부정)''는 반대 의미. ③ very와 ④ quite는 enough와 이런 구조로 쓰이지 않습니다.','형용사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1m000se3wcpw4sc9by',5,'Conference participants _______ to register at least two weeks before the event to guarantee seating.','require','are required','requiring','have required','B','[수동태 be required to] 참가자들이 요구를 ''받는'' 입장이므로 수동태가 필요합니다. are required to = ''~해야 한다(의무)''. ① require는 능동태로 참가자들이 누군가에게 요구한다는 의미. ③ requiring은 단독으로 술어 동사가 될 수 없습니다. ④ have required는 능동 현재완료입니다.','수동태',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqb0n1n000te3wc8ltkpnmw',5,'The company''s office hours will change _______ 8:30 A.M. to 7:30 A.M. starting the first Monday of next month.','since','between','from','during','C','[from A to B] ''from A to B''는 ''시작점(A)에서 끝점(B)으로의 변화''를 나타냅니다. from 8:30 A.M. to 7:30 A.M. = ''8시 30분에서 7시 30분으로 변경''. ② between은 ''between A and B'' 구조여야 합니다. ① since는 현재완료와 함께 ''이후로'', ④ during은 ''~동안''으로 변화의 시작점 표현에 맞지 않습니다.','전치사',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q20000uswcadt99kj6',5,'The facility manager announced that all employees must _______ the new safety regulations by the end of the month.','complying to','complied by','compliance in','comply with','D','[comply with] ''comply with''는 ''~을 준수하다''는 고정 표현입니다. ① complying to는 동사 자리에 -ing는 부적절하고 전치사도 틀렸습니다. ② complied by는 수동 구조이며 문맥에 맞지 않습니다. ③ compliance는 명사로 동사 자리에 올 수 없습니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q70001uswc50w5im5p',5,'The quarterly earnings report revealed a _______ increase in revenue compared to the same period last year.','remark','remarked','remarkable','remarkably','C','[형용사] 관사 a와 명사 increase 사이에는 형용사(remarkable)가 필요합니다. ④ remarkably는 부사로 명사를 수식할 수 없습니다. ① remark는 동사/명사로 이 자리에 부적절합니다. ② remarked는 과거형 동사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q80002uswchob0c6zc',5,'Ms. Thornton has _______ more than fifteen years of experience in international trade law.','accumulating','accumulated','accumulately','accumulation','B','[현재완료 동사] has 뒤에는 과거분사(p.p.)가 옵니다. accumulated는 accumulate의 과거분사입니다. ③ 부사 형태이며 잘못된 단어입니다. ④ accumulation은 명사입니다. ① has + -ing는 현재진행 시제가 되어 의미가 다릅니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q80003uswc11n8ui09',5,'The new branch will open its doors _______ completing a comprehensive renovation of the historic building.','following','followed','follows','follow','A','[전치사 following] following은 ''~에 뒤이어, ~후에''를 의미하는 전치사로, 뒤에 명사/동명사를 취합니다. ② followed는 동사의 과거형입니다. ③ follows는 3인칭 단수 현재형입니다. ④ follow는 동사원형입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q90004uswcst7emhhl',5,'All applications submitted _______ the posted deadline will not be considered for the position.','until','since','during','after','D','[after] ''마감일 이후에 제출된 지원서는 고려되지 않는다''는 문맥이므로 after가 적절합니다. ① until은 ''~까지''로 기간의 끝을 나타냅니다. ② since는 ''~이후로''이지만 현재완료와 함께 쓰입니다. ③ during은 ''~하는 동안''입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q90005uswca47btg4q',5,'The regional director praised the sales team for _______ their annual target three months ahead of schedule.','to exceed','excess','exceeding','exceeded','C','[전치사 for 뒤 동명사] for 뒤에는 동명사(-ing)가 옵니다. exceeding(초과하다)의 동명사입니다. ④ exceeded는 과거형 동사입니다. ① to exceed는 to부정사로 전치사 뒤에 올 수 없습니다. ② excess는 명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56q90006uswcn4suajny',5,'_______ the software update has been installed, users will notice a significant improvement in processing speed.','Instead','Once','Despite','Whereas','B','[Once] Once는 ''~하고 나면, 일단 ~하면''의 의미로 조건/시간 부사절을 이끄는 접속사입니다. ③ Despite는 전치사로 뒤에 명사/동명사가 옵니다. ④ Whereas는 ''반면에''로 대조를 나타냅니다. ① Instead는 부사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qa0007uswcitxdwrhk',5,'The marketing team''s _______ use of social media platforms contributed to a 40% increase in brand awareness.','strategic','strategically','strategy','strategize','A','[형용사] 관사 The와 명사 use 사이에서 명사를 수식하는 형용사(strategic)가 필요합니다. ② strategically는 부사입니다. ③ strategy는 명사이며 ''전략''이라는 의미로 여기서는 어색합니다. ④ strategize는 동사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qa0008uswcwfc3cq30',5,'The consultant recommended that the company _______ its pricing structure to remain competitive in the market.','revised','revising','revision','revise','D','[가정법 현재] recommend that + 주어 + 동사원형(should 생략 가능). 제안동사(recommend, suggest, require 등) 뒤에 오는 that절에서는 주어에 상관없이 동사원형을 씁니다. ① revised는 과거형입니다. ② revising은 진행형입니다. ③ revision은 명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qb0009uswcgdm2sxsc',5,'Mr. Nakamura is responsible for conducting the performance reviews _______ his entire department.','by','at','for','on','C','[for] ''~을 위한(대상)''을 나타낼 때 for를 씁니다. ''conduct reviews for a department''는 ''부서를 대상으로 리뷰를 진행하다''는 의미입니다. ④ on은 주제나 접촉을 나타냅니다. ① by는 수단이나 행위자를 나타냅니다. ② at은 위치나 시간을 나타냅니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qb000auswcc6baipgp',5,'The contract stipulates that neither the buyer _______ the seller may withdraw from the agreement without written notice.','but','nor','and','or','B','[neither A nor B] 상관 접속사 neither는 반드시 nor와 짝을 이룹니다. ''neither A nor B''는 ''A도 B도 ~아니다''의 의미입니다. ③ and는 either와 함께 쓰입니다. ④ or는 either와 함께 쓰입니다. ① but은 상관 접속사 neither와 함께 쓰이지 않습니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qc000buswcevdej4wv',5,'Customers who order online will receive _______ products at their doorstep within three business days.','their','them','they','themselves','A','[소유격] 명사 products 앞에서 소유를 나타내는 소유격 their(그들의)가 필요합니다. ② them은 목적격입니다. ③ they는 주격입니다. ④ themselves는 재귀대명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qc000cuswcptmf5du8',5,'The Hartwell Conference Center is _______ located near the city''s main transportation hub.','convenient','convenience','conveniences','conveniently','D','[부사] 동사 located를 수식하려면 부사 conveniently(편리하게)가 필요합니다. ① convenient는 형용사입니다. ②③ convenience는 명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qd000duswclxansnfy',5,'The newly _______ supervisor immediately began reorganizing the workflow to improve efficiency.','appoint','appointment','appointed','appointing','C','[과거분사 형용사 수식] newly 뒤에 과거분사 appointed(임명된)가 supervisor를 수식합니다. ④ appointing은 능동 분사로 ''임명하는''이 되어 의미가 맞지 않습니다. ① appoint는 동사원형입니다. ② appointment는 명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qd000euswcqkzldwfo',5,'Please note that our customer service office will be closed _______ the national public holiday next Monday.','whether','due to','in spite of','unless','B','[due to] due to는 ''~때문에''를 의미하는 전치사구로 뒤에 명사/명사구가 옵니다. ③ in spite of는 ''~에도 불구하고''로 반대되는 의미입니다. ④ unless는 접속사입니다. ① whether는 접속사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qe000fuswcz49getrw',5,'The researchers found that consumer behavior varies _______ depending on cultural backgrounds and income levels.','considerably','considerable','consider','consideration','A','[부사] 동사 varies를 수식하는 부사 considerably(상당히)가 적절합니다. ② considerable은 형용사입니다. ③ consider는 동사입니다. ④ consideration은 명사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qf000guswcmmj45av9',5,'All staff members wishing to attend the leadership seminar should submit _______ applications by Thursday.','his','its','your','their','D','[대명사 수 일치] all staff members(복수)를 받는 대명사는 복수형 their가 적절합니다. ① his는 남성 단수입니다. ② its는 사물을 가리킵니다. ③ your는 2인칭으로 문맥에 맞지 않습니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qf000huswcx18d5ip6',5,'The renovation project was completed well _______ the initial deadline, which exceeded all expectations.','instead of','in case of','ahead of','in front of','C','[ahead of] ''ahead of schedule/deadline''은 ''기한보다 일찍''이라는 관용 표현입니다. ④ in front of는 물리적인 위치(''앞에'')를 나타냅니다. ① instead of는 ''대신에''입니다. ② in case of는 ''~의 경우에''입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qg000iuswc115fj72x',5,'_______ applicants must complete a background check before being offered a permanent position.','Both','All','Every','Each','B','[All + 복수명사] All + 복수 명사는 집합 전체를 나타냅니다. ③ Every + 단수 명사, ④ Each + 단수 명사 — 이 문장에서 applicants가 복수이므로 모두 부적절합니다. ① Both는 정확히 두 명/개를 가리킬 때 사용합니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qh000juswca9jjrxxa',5,'The company''s new headquarters will be equipped _______ state-of-the-art security systems.','with','by','for','at','A','[be equipped with] ''be equipped with''는 ''~을 갖추다''는 고정 표현입니다. ② by는 행위자나 수단을 나타냅니다. ③ for는 목적이나 대상을 나타냅니다. ④ at은 장소나 시간을 나타냅니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qh000kuswc9tsskd4e',5,'Ms. Bergstrom''s presentation was so _______ that the board of directors immediately approved the proposal.','persuasively','persuasion','persuade','persuasive','D','[so + 형용사] ''so + 형용사 + that''은 ''너무 ~해서 …하다'' 구조입니다. so 뒤에는 형용사 persuasive(설득력 있는)가 옵니다. ① persuasively는 부사입니다. ② persuasion은 명사입니다. ③ persuade는 동사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qi000luswc2bi1p2bv',5,'The logistics team is _______ in ensuring all shipments arrive within the guaranteed delivery window.','instrument','instruct','instrumental','instrumentally','C','[be instrumental in] ''be instrumental in + 동명사''는 ''~에 중요한 역할을 하다''는 표현입니다. instrumental은 여기서 형용사로 사용됩니다. ④ instrumentally는 부사입니다. ① instrument는 명사입니다. ② instruct는 완전히 다른 의미의 동사입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qi000muswcy120se9u',5,'The vendor offered a 15 percent discount _______ the company placed an order for at least 500 units.','prior to','provided that','in spite of','as a result','B','[provided that] provided that은 ''~라는 조건 하에''를 의미하는 조건 접속사구입니다. ③ in spite of는 ''~에도 불구하고''로 의미가 반대입니다. ④ as a result는 부사구로 접속사 역할을 할 수 없습니다. ① prior to는 전치사구입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qj000nuswc64i0vqko',5,'The training manual should be read _______ before employees begin operating any of the new machinery.','thoroughly','thorough','thoroughness','thorough by','A','[부사 수식] 동사 read를 수식하는 부사 thoroughly(철저히)가 적절합니다. ② thorough는 형용사입니다. ③ thoroughness는 명사입니다. ④ thorough by는 잘못된 표현입니다.','',NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "Question" ("id","part","questionText","optionA","optionB","optionC","optionD","answer","explanation","category","groupId") VALUES ('cmqqc56qj000ouswczecaqatc',5,'Employees _______ travel for business purposes are entitled to a daily meal allowance of $50.','whose','which','what','who','D','[주격 관계대명사 who] 사람(Employees)을 선행사로 받고 관계절에서 주어 역할을 하는 who가 적절합니다. ① whose는 소유격 관계대명사입니다. ② which는 사물에 씁니다. ③ what은 선행사를 포함한 관계대명사로 여기에는 부적절합니다.','',NULL);

